\title{GeneCastR: Introduction Time and Spread of Genetic Variants Under Wright-Fisher Dynamics}
\description{
Fits a Wright-Fisher model with genic selection and recurrent gene flow to panels of allele-frequency surveys, with optional per-deme hierarchies over the growth advantage and the effective size, and reports projected frequencies, presence and exceedance probabilities, and posteriors over the introduction time and the founding time of the lineage that was detected. The latent allele count is held on a lattice, so the likelihood is evaluated exactly by a forward-backward pass with no particle approximation, and the introduction time is marginalised analytically.
}
\section{Pipeline}{

Three objects, in order. Each is documented on its own page.

\describe{
\item{\link{GCData}}{validates a survey panel onto the model's lattice.
One row per survey: \code{deme}, \code{time}, \code{x}, \code{n}.}
\item{\link{GCFit}}{runs blocked Metropolis-within-Gibbs against the
\strong{exact} likelihood. Because the likelihood is evaluated rather than
estimated, this is ordinary Metropolis-within-Gibbs and not a
pseudo-marginal scheme.}
\item{\link{GCProjection}}{smoothed curves, projections, presence and
exceedance probabilities and the introduction times, as one row per
deme and step. Built by \link{GCFit}\verb{$project()}.}
}

Plotting: \link{gc_plot_frequency}, \link{gc_plot_present}, \link{gc_plot_exceed},
\link{gc_plot_times}, \link{gc_plot_joint}, \link{gc_plot_trace}.
}

\section{The three introduction times}{

\verb{t*} is the founding parameter, obtained analytically from a backward row
the likelihood already builds, so it carries no Monte-Carlo error.
\code{T_first} is the first step the variant is present, which under the
default founding law is identically \verb{t*}. \code{T_est} is the start of the
excursion that produced the first detected count -- walk back from the
first non-zero survey until the deme is empty -- so it is bounded by that
detection and is undefined where there was none. It is a path functional,
needs sampled paths, and is the only expensive output. Their joint
distribution has the probability that the detected lineage is the
original arrival on its diagonal.
}

\section{Caveats worth reading first}{

\code{nu} is an arrival rate \emph{conditional on the deme being empty}, not a
rate of gene flow. \verb{t*} has no prior support beyond the observation window,
so projected presence is biased low in never-detected demes. \code{nu} and \code{A}
are shared across demes. Nothing here corrects for the ascertainment that
selects which demes enter a panel.
}

